Description: One Beat FX that works from the first press
 The DDJ-400 BEAT FX section acted on Effect Unit 1's *focused* effect, and
 Mixxx starts with none in focus (focused_effect 0), so ON/OFF switched a
 non-existent slot until BEAT < or > had been pressed to pick one. And
 LEVEL/DEPTH had soft takeover on the unit's mix, which Mixxx remembers
 between runs, so the knob did nothing until it had been swept past the old
 value ("turn it to zero first").
 .
 The mapping now drives Effect 1 only: BEAT < / > load the previous / next
 effect into it (as FX SELECT and SHIFT + FX SELECT do), ON/OFF toggles it,
 LEVEL/DEPTH sets the mix directly, SHIFT + LEVEL/DEPTH its meta (still with
 soft takeover). init() switches slots 2 and 3 off, since the skin no longer
 shows them. StandardEffectChain also puts the focus on the first effect when
 it comes up at 0, which covers a stale copy of the mapping in the user
 mapping folder (see browse-encoder-zoom.patch).
Author: Pioneered CI <pioneered-build@localhost>
Forwarded: no
---
